Z||000000||martin1875||11-10-2000||11:30 PM||||i am new to the forum and to fieros in general. i have just got an 86 se v6.it was wrecked in the front not to bad. brought it home and tried to start it. for some odd reason it had at least 6 or 8 quarts of oil in it. changed oil and spark plugs and started it. smoked real bad then backfired and wont start again.turns over real slow, have a good battery.i guess the timing chain is broken or has jumped a tooth.i dont know which line in the balancer is right the wide or the skinny one.i plan on pulling the whole engine a rebuilding it . does any one know where to get an overhaul kit, other than the fiero store ,there kits seem to be high in price, or to purchase an rebuilt engine if possible. is the perfomance kit fiero store offers an real improment over stock ,in horsepower. sorry for a long message i, thank you for any help you have to offer||||reg||4
Z||000001||Tom88gt||11-11-2000||12:05 AM||||I'd have to say that your better of buying a rebuilt engine over rebuilding the one you have.  Usually cheaper and easier.  An even better option is to buy a low milage 3.4 out of an early 90s Camaro or Firebird.  <BR>You could get one and do the minor mods to install it for about $1000 total. ||||reg||1
